/* book exam traps: pi = yip, never pi = wip. Air is 0.21 oxygen by mole but 0.23 by mass, so the mass fraction overstates pO2 by about 10 %. | Partial pressure uses the mixture volume V and the mixture temperature T. Putting a component's own volume into piV = niRuT is the classic mistake. | Mixing unit sets. Ru = 8.314 works with kPa, m³ and kmol, or with Pa, m³ and mol. Putting MPa with m³, or mol with kmol, shifts the answer by a factor of 1000. | The mole fractions must add to 1.00. If an analysis sums to 0.95, a component is missing, not a rounding error. | Amagat's partial volume is not the volume of the gas before mixing. It is the volume that gas would occupy alone at the final p and T. */
